\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.1.1}{\ignorespaces The four storage models. They describe the \emph  {same} tree; they differ in what a ``child'' physically is, whether you can step \emph  {upward} in $O(1)$, and how much memory the edges cost. Section~\ref {sec:c04-rooting} adds the fifth act: choosing which node is the root once you have an adjacency list.}}{235}{figure.caption.51}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:c04-models}{{4.1.1}{235}{The four storage models. They describe the \emph {same} tree; they differ in what a ``child'' physically is, whether you can step \emph {upward} in $O(1)$, and how much memory the edges cost. Section~\ref {sec:c04-rooting} adds the fifth act: choosing which node is the root once you have an adjacency list}{figure.caption.51}{}}
